# Rulebook PDFs — 184 MB of binaries that never change, and commercial books
# besides. The tools that read them take a path; they do not need to be here.
*.pdf

# Compiled compendiums. The content lives in src/packs/ and packs/ is built
# from it — `node tools/build.mjs`. Committing the built LevelDB would also
# mean committing its LOCK file, which the running Foundry server holds open,
# so `git add` fails outright whenever the world is up.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: without it this pattern matches a `packs`
# directory at ANY depth, and silently swallows src/packs/ — 530 files of the
# actual source content — while looking exactly like it works.
/packs/

# Scratch: PDF text dumps, page renders, one-off compendium copies. Everything
# in here is regenerable and none of it is input to a build.
tmp/

# Local tool state, not project content. .claude/ in particular holds this
# machine's permission settings and can pick up local paths and tokens.
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/

# OS and editor litter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
